field (that is, /?), and one range and/or hash index to the vehicle path and all the nodes
under it (that is, /*). The hash index type is the index that's used for equality queries, while
the range index type is used for comparison or sorting.
By using the correct index paths and types, query costs can be decreased and scan queries
can be avoided. If the indexing mode is set to None instead of Consistent, the database
returns an error on the given collection. The queries can still be executed using the
EnableScanInQuery flag.
